1
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:13,620
Extend arms and bend wrists
at precisely 90 degrees,

2
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,532
making sure to keep each finger straight.

3
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:25,120
Then palms up in front, straighten elbows,

4
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,857
whilst maintaining the 90
degree angles, bend each finger.

5
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,960
One, two, three, four, five.

6
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:34,817
Now open your hands back up.

7
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,057
One, two, three, four, five.

8
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:39,520
And done?

9
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,437
Now you are ready to draw manga.

10
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,900
Let's begin, shall we?

11
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:02,500
Thank you.

12
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:38,997
Let's talk about your summer
deadline, Rohan-sensei.

13
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:42,777
I hope you haven't forgotten about
the 45-page one-shot, do you?

14
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,272
Have you at least settled on a story yet?

15
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,720
Hmm. One moment.

16
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:53,260
A solar eclipse might be
a good theme. Oh, yeah!

17
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,660
That's an amazing hook! I love it!

18
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:57,757
But you know what else sounds cool?

19
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:02,781
What if you drew for us a manga about buying
a beautiful holiday villa in the hills?

20
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,940
Sorry, come again?

21
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,751
It doesn't look like you're into the idea.

22
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,416
That's such a shame.

23
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,045
Now you hold on just a minute.

24
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,997
I need you to explain what you
meant by a villa in the hills.

25
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,617
It was an idea for a story,

26
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,417
but like you could also
totally go and do it for real

27
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,337
and see if maybe a bolt of
inspiration strikes you.

28
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:28,250
Enough!

29
00:02:28,333 --> 00:02:30,297
Stop acting like you
don't know what I mean.

30
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:32,837
I took issue with the buying
part of what you said.

31
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:35,117
You know full well that
I recently declared

32
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,777
bankruptcy due to a purchase
of that very nature.

33
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:41,920
Rohan Sensei, I don't want anything
from you other than a good story.

34
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:44,800
Here, look at this.

35
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:47,400
Quite the discovery, huh?

36
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:51,397
It's a little village nestled in
the hills with no connecting roads.

37
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:54,127
And yet it's got about
a dozen luxury villas.

38
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,897
I bet you never would
have guessed there was a

39
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:00,100
place like this just a few
hours northwest of Morioh.

40
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,937
It's so weird seeing
such a developed patch

41
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:05,540
of land without any roads or power lines.

42
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:11,562
They're not hooked up to a power
grid or any other public utility.

43
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:15,015
Yet they've got working
electricity and transportation.

44
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:17,237
Judging from all those helipads,

45
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,977
I'm going to assume that these
people get around mainly by air.

46
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:21,060
You may be right.

47
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,037
It certainly seems like
they can afford it.

48
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:27,397
And is it me, or does that building by
the tennis court have an Isetan logo?

49
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,320
Wow, it does!

50
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,597
They have one there?

51
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:30,540
Good for them!

52
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,100
Oh, and one more thing.

53
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:36,920
At the moment, one of those
villas is accessible to you.

54
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,338
That's right, for three million yen.

55
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,577
So, you finally admit you're
selling me real estate.

56
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,520
Still wrong. Trust me.

57
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,957
The only thing I want you to do is draw.

58
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,440
The one buying a house will be me.

59
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,540
You? Now let's see.

60
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,780
That's 2,600 square meters
going for 3 million yen.

61
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:07,394
On my salary, I could probably get a
loan for it or even buy it outright.

62
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:09,194
Yeah, this could work.

63
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:11,437
I could commute from my
apartment during the week,

64
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:15,017
then retreat to the countryside and kick
back during the weekend and holidays.

65
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,257
Slow down for a sec.

66
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:17,337
You forced me to ask.

67
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:21,244
Is this coming out of your pocket
or from the publishing company?

68
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,637
I was planning to do
this with my own money.

69
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,537
So I'm to draw a manga about you.

70
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:28,457
Nope, once again, this is
all to inspire you, silly.

71
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:31,011
Look, I've put a lot of thought into this.

72
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:34,512
And I'll share with you all
the info I dug up to prove it.

73
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,837
The owner of Villa No.

74
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:39,567
1 is the president of
a shipbuilding company.

75
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:40,650
No.

76
00:04:40,733 --> 00:04:42,020
2 belongs to a pharma CEO.

77
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,597
While the guy in No.

78
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,209
3 owns a printing company.

79
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:48,578
And the guy in number four
runs a cosmetics business.

80
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,857
Needless to say, all the people living
here are fancy-pants millionaire types.

81
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:55,380
With their trophy wives and cute kids?

82
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:57,377
Sounds like a dream, doesn't it?

83
00:04:57,460 --> 00:05:01,813
Collecting data is one thing, but
making sense of it all is quite another.

84
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:05,567
For starters, how does a villa
here go for only three million?

85
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:07,960
There must be a catch.

86
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,817
Except there isn't, Rohan-sensei.

87
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:13,606
I've yet to tell you the most
important thing about this place.

88
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:17,417
The 11 people who live here
they all bought their lots

89
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:21,157
when they were just 25 years
old can you Believe it I mean

90
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,857
yeah they're super loaded
today but all of them came up

91
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:26,937
from humble beginnings The
most recent arrival in this

92
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:30,297
village bought his plot of
land number 11 back in 1989

93
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:34,437
the man Was a modest 25 year
old delivery driver who had

94
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:38,177
moved all the way out there
from tokyo And now he's the head

95
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:41,840
honcho of a big airline company
worth over 30 billion yen

96
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:47,147
So yeah, there's not a single person
living in this village who came for money.

97
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:51,037
They were all just ordinary
25-year-old dudes who moved

98
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:54,532
out here one by one and built
up their fortunes over time.

99
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:58,936
And you've probably noticed, but it
looks like there's a common number.

100
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:03,640
As it happens, I'm also
25 years old. Get it now?

101
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,640
There's clearly a story here.

102
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:10,234
Now be honest, don't you want to come
see me get a lucky villa of my own?

103
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,991
I'm assuming you have access to a chopper.

104
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,218
I can't see how else we'd get there.

105
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:07,977
Rohan Sensei, there's one more important
detail I forgot to mention earlier.

106
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:12,337
The seller is the head of the village
council, and they're very fussy about decorum.

107
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,237
I've heard they're dead set
against selling their land

108
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:17,477
to anyone whom they think
comes across as disrespectful.

109
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,997
Proper manners will make
all the difference today.

110
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:22,609
So, I hope you'll be
on your best behavior.

111
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:28,660
I fail to see how my conduct will endanger
anything when the only buyer is you.

112
00:07:28,940 --> 00:07:29,840
Okay, fine.

113
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,897
I'll just spell it out for you.

114
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:34,557
It doesn't matter which one
of us commits the faux pas,

115
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,877
they'll just lump us together
and toss us both out.

116
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:40,117
And I don't want to leave
empty-handed after that hike.

117
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,177
Seriously, though,

118
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:43,897
I don't know if anyone's
ever told you this before,

119
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:48,157
but you always act like some hotshot diva
who's addicted to his own flatulence.

120
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,070
Oh, come on.

121
00:07:49,153 --> 00:07:50,157
What does that even mean?

122
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:52,597
It means stop worshipping
yourself and be a good boy,

123
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:56,327
or the locals will boot us before
you can smell one more fart.

124
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:57,862
Here's an idea.

125
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,904
Let's practice before we go in.

126
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:05,454
Traditionally, where in the house
should a visitor take their jacket off?

127
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:08,740
You seem set on wasting my
time with this nonsense.

128
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:11,440
The answer is at the entrance.

129
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:13,500
Not once you've come inside?

130
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,817
But before you pass through the door!

131
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:18,437
just in case there's
lingering dirt on your coat.

132
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:19,350
What a relief!

133
00:08:19,433 --> 00:08:20,817
So you do know how to behave!

134
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,730
Wait,

135
00:08:21,813 --> 00:08:23,677
I understand this visit takes precedence,

136
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:26,466
but perhaps we should
do something about that.

137
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:29,380
I mean that chick over there.

138
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:33,620
Poor thing.

139
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:37,957
The simplest explanation would be
that it fell down from its nest.

140
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,099
What should we do?

141
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,937
If we leave him, he might
get eaten by something.

142
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:43,260
Or freeze to death.

143
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:47,720
Well, if that happens, we could
simply write it off as nature's work.

144
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,155
Good thing we found you, little Fool.

145
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:53,187
Don't worry, we'll help you.

146
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:56,520
I'm glad I hung on to
this box. There you go.

147
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,377
It's likely his nest is
in one of these trees.

148
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:02,989
We should come back
here later and find it.

149
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,337
Good day to you.

150
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:19,757
I'd like to begin by thanking
you for coming all this way.

151
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:24,137
And I'm glad to see that good weather
was accommodating to your long journey.

152
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:25,400
This way, please.

153
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:27,517
We've been waiting.

154
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,600
Let us proceed swiftly.

155
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,497
My name is Kyoka Izumi.

156
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:40,277
Thank you so much for sparing
us some of your precious

157
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,437
time to discuss the sale
of your lovely estate.

158
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:45,537
This gentleman here is my
good friend Rohan Kishibe.

159
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,337
He's a successful manga artist.

160
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,797
I'm pleased to meet you.

161
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,017
You may call me IQ.

162
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:52,537
I've been given the great honor.

163
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:54,561
of facilitating your visit today.

164
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,680
Please follow me as I guide you.

165
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:13,160
Now then, if you would kindly allow
me to relieve you of your coats.

166
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,535
Please, you may enter at your leisure.

167
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:40,770
Hey!

168
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:56,957
In just a moment, I shall go fetch the
seller with whom you will transact.

169
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,687
Make yourselves comfortable.

170
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:48,760
I'm beginning to suspect that the test
has already been put into motion, right?

171
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:52,520
I'm talking about our etiquette.

172
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:55,208
There may be rules
surrounding tea drinking,

173
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:58,439
and they're waiting to see
how we approach our cups.

174
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:01,972
Somehow, I get the feeling
we're being observed right now.

175
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:05,152
Do you know the proper way of proceeding?

176
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:10,034
Or should I just go straight
to consulting the internet?

177
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,740
No, it's fine.

178
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:14,597
As the buyer, I should
be able to handle this.

179
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,033
Don't trouble yourself.

180
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:20,968
Everyone knows the polite way of drinking
is quietly and without acting weird.

181
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:34,600
Excuse the intrusion.

182
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:41,400
I sincerely regret to inform
you of this, but sadly,

183
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:44,835
the seller is no longer
interested in meeting with you.

184
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:47,432
I must ask you to leave the premises now.

185
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:52,501
It pains me to say it, but we cannot
abide your etiquette mistakes.

186
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,640
Miss Izumi.

187
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:57,939
We have no land to sell to
anyone who lacks manners.

188
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,177
Please return home for today.

189
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:01,777
Wait, what are you talking about?

190
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:02,690
What did I...

191
00:13:02,773 --> 00:13:05,160
What did I do wrong? Firstly,

192
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,137
though you are a guest in this house,

193
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:09,337
it is improper to take the
furthest seat from the door!

194
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:11,067
unless it is offered to you.

195
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,607
You should take the closest.

196
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:20,517
You are expected to remain there until you
have been properly greeted by the host.

197
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,440
Secondly,

198
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:26,332
it is improper to tread on the edges
of the tatami mats in a Japanese room.

199
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:31,640
And third,

200
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:34,737
when sitting at a table lower
than the level of your knees,

201
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:37,480
it is correct to hold
your tea by the saucer.

202
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:44,040
However, to put your finger through the
handle of the teacup is unspeakably vulgar.

203
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:51,440
Good etiquette is a simple organization
of shoulds and should-nots.

204
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:53,080
There is no gray area.

205
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:55,800
Again, I must ask you to return home.

206
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,462
You mean we're finished already?

207
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:00,520
Wait a moment. Please.

208
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,998
You said it's just for today, right?

209
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:05,217
Does that mean it'd be
possible for me to try again?

210
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:07,837
Because if it does, I'd
sincerely appreciate it.

211
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,780
I'll give it this time. What?

212
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:10,877
Just one more try.

213
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:14,337
If it's not too much to ask, I
promise I won't disappoint you again.

214
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,457
Please let me prove it.

215
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:18,217
So you would like to attempt
the trial one more time.

216
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:20,124
Did I understand you correctly?

217
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,540
Only if that's okay.

218
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:24,060
Very well, then.

219
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:28,931
If that's the case, I will present your
request to the Master for an answer.

220
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:30,840
Thank you. Please do.

221
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,745
I promise you won't regret it.

222
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,500
Hey, let's just leave.

223
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:37,597
There aren't any good manga
ideas to be found here.

224
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:40,856
I would leave if I weren't
so in love with this place.

225
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,657
Sure, they're strict about etiquette,

226
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:46,460
but that's what I'd expect
just just look around you.

227
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:48,180
It's so lovely

228
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,720
Hi, Kyoka speaking

229
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,480
What the hell happened?

230
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:11,790
Oh, no!

231
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:16,780
No, please, no!

232
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,717
I have to...

233
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:22,640
I just got news my mother was killed.

234
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:25,957
They said that she...

235
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:30,600
There was a car accident,
and she didn't make it.

236
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:36,280
My boyfriend was there, too.

237
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:39,097
We were making plans to
finally get married next year,

238
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:42,057
But he was in the car with
my mother at the time.

239
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:45,081
Then she suddenly got a
heart attack at the wheel.

240
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:46,400
I can't...

241
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:51,300
They've both been taken from me!

242
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,200
What is going on?

243
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:55,380
Where did these insects come from?

244
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,020
Excuse the intrusion.

245
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:03,978
The Master has agreed to let you
take the trial of manners once again.

246
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,540
Now let us proceed.

247
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:08,620
You will reveal yourself this instant!

248
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:12,940
Heaven's door!

249
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:22,800
I am the guide at the main gate,
and the land speaks through me.

250
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:24,697
When crossing into this domain,

251
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:26,777
those lacking proper
etiquette will soon find

252
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:29,919
themselves also lacking
something that they cherish.

253
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:33,877
Without exception, this is
the punishment of the hill.

254
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:36,277
One will gain, or one will lose.

255
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:40,520
That is the fundamental rule
which governs this land.

256
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:43,724
Those proficient in
etiquette will gain success.

257
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:46,277
Those who are not will
suffer for each offense.

258
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,640
This young man is no stand user.

259
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:52,137
It seems he's little more than a
guide and mouthpiece for these beings,

260
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,377
with no special abilities of his own.

261
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:55,780
This bodes terribly.

262
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:59,500
It appears our enemies
are the gods of the hill.

263
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:03,237
For the three rules she
broke, she lost three things.

264
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:06,817
She then further transgressed when
she begged for another chance.

265
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:07,730
Impudence.

266
00:17:07,813 --> 00:17:12,197
On top of that, turning
someone into a book?

267
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,157
and reading their mind without permission!

268
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:17,280
is also an egregious act of disrespect!

269
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:19,320
Oh, no!

270
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:21,220
You're kidding!

271
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,500
This... this is bad!

272
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:31,150
My...

273
00:17:31,233 --> 00:17:32,063
my chest!

274
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:43,800
It appears Miss Izumi is currently
suffering a heart attack.

275
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:45,390
Mr.

276
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,380
Rohan Kishibe,

277
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:50,738
you have broken one rule of etiquette,
and so you will lose one thing.

278
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:55,040
Tell me, do you intend
for her to die? You first.

279
00:17:55,780 --> 00:18:00,620
Do you intend to continue with the trial,
or would you prefer to return home now?

280
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,840
You know I can't. Not anymore.

281
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,660
I won't leave her here.

282
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,141
Please, I beg of you, have mercy!

283
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:12,697
Her only transgression was
yearning for a chance at happiness!

284
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:17,545
I know now that when she said she wanted
to help me with my work, it was sincere.

285
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,177
Mercy is outside the realm of etiquette.

286
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:24,860
Here you will either gain,
or you will suffer loss.

287
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:28,920
Now, what is the proper
way to eat a cob of corn?

288
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:33,700
Well, would you care to
try once more, Mr. Kishibe?

289
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:37,980
Again, you are free to return
home whenever you wish.

290
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:08,840
Don't underestimate Rohan Kishibe.

291
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:11,748
The utensils you've
laid out here before me.

292
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:15,725
It is obvious that none of them
are suited for the task at hand.

293
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,600
Behold as I answer you!

294
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:20,730
Satisfied yet?

295
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:22,100
There's more.

296
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:28,000
You should brace yourself first, and
then look down when you're ready.

297
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:36,368
Who's the rule-breaker now?

298
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:39,217
I mean, I'll admit, this
isn't the plot I envisioned.

299
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:43,065
But given the tight deadline, it
was the best one I could write.

300
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:47,020
I'm speaking of my ability.

301
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:48,410
Heaven's door.

302
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:53,120
Oh, look.

303
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,634
You're doing it again.

304
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:56,260
It's both feet.

305
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,529
It's an impressive
power, wouldn't you say?

306
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:04,240
I do appreciate the lessons
you gave me. Thank you.

307
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:08,140
Now, on to the matter of what
I gain, as per the rules.

308
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,089
Seems my answer was right.

309
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:17,245
The proper way to eat a
cob of corn is by hand.

310
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:20,077
I think you owe my
colleague something as well.

311
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:22,101
Her beloved mother and boyfriend.

312
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:24,557
This is an obscene trick. You...

313
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,816
you will incur the wrath of the gods.

314
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:28,530
Mr.

315
00:20:28,613 --> 00:20:31,260
Kishibe, will you be
making another attempt?

316
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:35,420
Or would you prefer to call it
a day and return home? My, my.

317
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:37,917
It seems the gods have no quarrel with me.

318
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,917
And why would they, considering
you're the one who violated the rules?

319
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,740
I choose to go home.

320
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:46,340
And I don't intend to return.

321
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:14,380
Wow, that's one heck of a story.

322
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,230
Oh yeah,

323
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:20,277
so do you know what ended up happening to
the editor lady's mother and boyfriend?

324
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,957
They were both perfectly fine.

325
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,237
They were merely rear-ended,
which panicked a relative,

326
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:26,557
who then proceeded to sound a false alarm.

327
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:27,960
That is such a relief.

328
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:32,100
By the way, Koichi, I have
some research to do after this,

329
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,357
and likely won't be back
until well after eight.

330
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:35,270
Okay.

331
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:37,596
So, you're gonna go do research, huh?

332
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:41,192
I hope you're looking up a way
to stop being a freeloader.

333
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,897
You make a very good point.

334
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:46,557
I should work on finding a new
place where I can draw freely.

335
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:48,111
Sadly, I'm utterly broke.

336
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:50,077
Do you want to come to my place?

337
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:52,689
We got plenty of rooms
you could set up in.

338
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:54,810
Huh?

339
00:21:54,893 --> 00:21:55,760
That does sound nice.

340
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:00,120
As it happens, your father is
a topic of interest for me.

341
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:01,520
Wait, really?

342
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:02,937
You want to do today, then?

343
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:05,017
Maybe your heavens-whatever
can turn him back.

344
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:06,120
Could you try it?

345
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:08,300
I must refuse. What?

346
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:29,377
To chain a mystic rise.

347
00:22:29,460 --> 00:22:31,497
I'm coming.

348
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:34,817
I'm on my way to find.

349
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:37,557
Eternal valedictives.

350
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:41,377
Exploding all their teardrops by the sun.

351
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:48,137
I can feel my heart feeling.

352
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:51,997
I can see my face.

353
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:54,897
All spinning round.

354
00:22:54,980 --> 00:22:57,540
Beyond the storm.

355
00:22:58,900 --> 00:23:01,957
Rise up to the sky.

356
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:04,177
Like a butterfly.

357
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:07,277
Show me what's inside.

358
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:09,857
Don't know the world grow.

359
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:13,617
Shining stars will guide me to.

360
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:15,477
Somewhere high.

361
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,037
Finding the truth.

362
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:19,740
Beyond the heaven storm.

363
00:23:54,980 --> 00:24:00,600
Thank you.
